{"type":"npc","name":"Living Lightning Rod","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":250,"temp":0,"max":250,"details":""},"ac":{"value":37,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":20,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"electricity","exceptions":[]},{"type":"mental","exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"sonic","value":15,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":[],"details":""},"level":{"value":15},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Relics of a bygone age, living lightning rods once served as guardians for a long-lost civilization. Records show that this civilization angered a capricious storm deity, and the deity smote these ancient peoples with devastating bolts of thunder. In response, the people created living lightning rods to protect the land until the god's anger subsided.</p><p>Living lightning rods are not hostile by nature, but each guards a particular monument or relic of their creators and responds violently to perceived vandals. While these constructs typically remain motionless until forced to respond, they can occasionally be found wandering through storms, waiting to be recharged by an errant lightning strike.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 810/1,850/3,400 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (heavy), perception item, skill items (Athletics)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, constitution, electricity, elongating, energy resistant (electricity, sonic, spirit, vitality, void), metal, sensory (darkvision), strength, throwing, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Jackson Walsh","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":9},"dex":{"mod":6},"con":{"mod