ightning rod is @UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.effects.Item.Bi2aHykg6CZrQCnR]{Charged 2} at the beginning of the encounter.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"interaction","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"7xwX8oQqsoJ8gORo","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"name":"Charged","type":"effect","effects":[],"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The charged condition always has a value, from 1 to 3. If a charged creature is already charged and would become charged, they instead increase the value of their charged condition by 1 to a maximum of charged 3. A charged creature is @UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.effects.Item.1fZbuJEbVmE3J4XL]{shocked} as long as it is charged. Any effect that would remove the shocked condition instead reduces the charged condition value by 1.</p>"},"rules":[{"key":"GrantItem","uuid":"Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.effects.Item.1fZbuJEbVmE3J4XL","flag":"shocked"}],"slug":"charged","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Eldamon","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":1},"duration":{"value":-1,"unit":"unlimited","expiry":null,"sustained":false},"start":{"value":6,"initiative":null},"tokenIcon":{"show":true},"badge":{"type":"counter","value":2,"max":3,"labels":null,"loop":false,"min":null},"context":{"origin":{"actor":"Actor.MZYS3YF9i5hdCkCL","token":null,"item":"Actor.MZYS3YF9i5hdCkCL.Item.7xwX8oQqsoJ8gORo","spellcasting":null,"rollOptions":[]},"target":null,"roll":null},"unidentified":false,"fromSpell":false},"img":"icons/magic/lightning/fist-unarmed-strike-blue-green.webp","folder":"e87TCAxSogrSh3km","flags":{"core":{},"pf2e":{"itemGrants":{"shocked":{"id":"7w5tKC2eOIBGf5Jf","onDelete":"detach"}}}},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.effects.Item.Bi2aHykg6CZrQCnR","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"_id":"w3SJrGMJzQid8G3g"},{"name":"Shocked","type":"effect","effects":[],"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The shocked condition normally doesn't have a value. A shocked creature is electrically charged, making it easy for electricity to harm it. It's @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AJh5ex99aV6VTggg]{Off-Guard} against attacks that deal electricity damage (even if it's only additional electricity damage, such as a <em>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.NVst7e69agGG9Qwd]{Shock}</em> weapon) and takes –2 circumstance penalty on Fortitude and Reflex saving throws against electricity effects.</p>\n<p>The shocked condition normally lasts for the duration listed, but it ends early if the creature takes any amount of electricity damage from a source other than persistent electricity damage, or if they spend an Interact action to discharge the electricity harmlessly.</p>"},"rules":[{"key":"FlatModifier","selector":["fortitude","reflex"],"value":-2,"predicate":["item:trait:electricity"],"type":"circumstance"}],"slug":"shocked","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Eldamon","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":1},"duration":{"value":-1,"unit":"unlimited","expiry":null,"sustained":false},"start":{"value":6,"initiativ